# Local development only.
#
# Production is a file upload to cPanel, which runs its own Apache and never
# reads this file — so there is no real domain to put here. It used to say
# "yourdomain.com", which answered for nothing and made it look as though the
# site was served through Caddy.
#
# ":80" means plain HTTP on any hostname. Do not name a real domain: Caddy
# would go straight out to Let's Encrypt for a certificate on startup, which
# cannot succeed on a laptop (public DNS does not point at it) and leaves the
# site unreachable while it retries.
#
# Day to day you do not need this at all — docker-compose.yml publishes the web
# container on http://localhost:8080 directly.
:80 {
	reverse_proxy web:80
}
